{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Charge_Battery","to":"Charge Battery"},{"from":"Dark_Embrace","to":"Dark Embrace"},{"from":"Cold_Snap","to":"Cold Snap"},{"from":"Wraith_Form","to":"Wraith Form"},{"from":"Flying_Knee","to":"Flying Knee"},{"from":"Simmering_Fury","to":"Simmering Fury"},{"from":"Dual_Wield","to":"Dual Wield"},{"from":"Creative_AI","to":"Creative AI"}],"pages":{"2128":{"pageid":2128,"ns":0,"title":"Auto-Shields","revisions":[{"revid":56886,"parentid":55628,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Auto-Shields\n|Image       = Blue-Auto-Shields.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = If you have no {{KW|Block}}, gain (11;15) {{KW|Block}}.\n|InteractsWith = Block\n|GivesToPlayer = Block\n}}\n{{C|Auto-Shields}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. <!-- It gives 11 (15 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}}, with the caveat that it will not give any {{KW|Block}} if you already have {{KW|Block}}. -->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{KW|Block}} carried over from the previous turn through {{R|Calipers}} will cause this card to have no effect.\n\n* Any {{KW|Block}} gained before playing {{C|Auto-Shields}} will cause it to have no effect, unless the {{KW|Block}} gained is removed in the meantime, such as through {{BD|Thorns}} or {{BD|Beat of Death}}. This means that:\n** {{C|Auto-Shields}} does not synergize with itself. In the same way, playing it multiple times with {{C|Echo Form}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}} gives the same amount of {{KW|Block}} as simply playing it once.\n** Using {{C|Hologram}} to place {{C|Auto-Shields}} back in hand will cause {{C|Auto-Shields}} to have no effect.\n** Any activation of {{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}} before playing {{C|Auto-Shields}} will cause it to have no effect. {{BD|Loop}} or {{R|Emotion Chip}} can trigger the passive ability of a {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}} at the start of your turn, while {{C|Coolheaded}} or {{C|Fission|upgraded Fission}} can {{KW|Evoke}} {{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}} while drawing {{C|Auto-Shields}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1900":{"pageid":1900,"ns":0,"title":"Berserk","revisions":[{"revid":56432,"parentid":55645,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Berserk\n| Image       = Red-Berserk.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Gain (2;1) {{BD|Vulnerable}}.<br>At the start of your turn, gain {{Icon|RE}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Vulnerable, Energy\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Berserk\n| Image        = Icon Berserk.png\n| Description  = At the start of your turn, gain X {{Icon|RE}} Energy.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToPlayer = Energy\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}}\n{{C|Berserk}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|Berserk}}, which gives that amount of {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' at the start of every turn. It debuffs you with 2 (1 if upgraded) {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Odd Mushroom}} reduces the severity of the {{BD|Vulnerable}} you get from this card.\n* {{R|Orange Pellets}} can remove the {{BD|Vulnerable}} you get from this card.\n* Sources of {{BD|Artifact}}, such as {{R|Clockwork Souvenir}}, {{P|Ancient Potion}}, {{C|Core Surge}} and {{C|Panacea}} can prevent this card from applying {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Berserk card buffed. Self Vulnerable 3 -> 2.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Berserk power.\n** Fix for Berserk card crash.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Berserk card buff: Cost 1 -> 0. Upgrading now reduces Vulnerable from 3 -> 2.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 33: Terror'''\n** Berserk card buffed. Applies 3 Vulnerable to self instead of 5.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Rework: Berserk card: Gain Vulnerable for several turns to gain +1 Energy per turn.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Meat on the Bone, Red Skull, Slime's Split, and Berserk all trigger on less than or equal to 50% HP and desc are updated to reflect this\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Berserk Card buffed.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2438":{"pageid":2438,"ns":0,"title":"Blind","revisions":[{"revid":56901,"parentid":55653,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Blind\n|Image       = Colorless-Blind.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Apply 2 {{BD|Weak}}(; to ALL enemies).\n|GivesToEnemy = Weak\n}} \n{{Power Infobox|Weak}}\n{{C|Blind}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It applies 2 {{BD|Weak}} to the target, or to '''ALL''' enemies if upgraded.\n\n== Obtaining Blind ==\n{{C|Blind}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Blind can now upgrade (Single Target -> All enemies)\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1905":{"pageid":1905,"ns":0,"title":"Brutality","revisions":[{"revid":56434,"parentid":55670,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Brutality\n| Image       = Red-Brutality.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = (;{{KW|Innate}}.<br>)At the start of your turn, lose 1 HP and draw 1 card.\n| GivesToPlayer = Lose HP, Draw, Innate\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Brutality}}{{C|Brutality}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|Brutality}}, which costs that amount of HP and draws that amount of cards at the start of every turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Tungsten Rod}} completely negates the damage from the first stack of {{BD|Brutality}}.\n* {{C|Brutality}} can be used to reliably and repeatedly trigger {{C|Rupture}}, {{R|Runic Cube}} and {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}, and lower the cost of {{C|Blood for Blood}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Brutality}} can trigger {{R|Centennial Puzzle}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating icon for Brutality power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Brutality Card buffed.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2061":{"pageid":2061,"ns":0,"title":"Charge Battery","revisions":[{"revid":56934,"parentid":53377,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Charge Battery\n|Image       = Blue-ChargeBattery.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (7;10) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Next turn, gain {{Icon|BE}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Energized (Defect), Block\n|PowerGives = Energy\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Power Infobox|Energized (Defect)}}\n{{C|Charge Battery}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The card art seems to depict the {{R|Cracked Core}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Adding beta art for Bane, Charge Battery, Fission, Choke, Corpse Explosion, and Equilibrium.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Conserve Battery card renamed to Charge Battery.\n** Conserve Battery card now gives energy next turn rather than conserve it.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2453":{"pageid":2453,"ns":0,"title":"Chrysalis","revisions":[{"revid":56937,"parentid":55694,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Chrysalis\n|Image       = Colorless-Chrysalis.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Shuffle (3;5) random Skills into your draw pile. They cost 0 this combat.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Chrysalis}} is a 2 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It shuffles 3 (5 if upgraded) random {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} cards into your draw pile, which will have their normal cost replaced by 0 for this combat, after which this {{C|Chrysalis}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. \n\n{{C|Chrysalis}} can only generate cards you can find in card rewards through character choice or custom run modifiers, and is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}}. If you use the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} [[Custom Mode#Daily Modifiers|Modifier]], this card has a chance to generate itself, meaning you can theorethically keep generating {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} cards infinitely using this card. \n\n== Obtaining Chrysalis ==\n{{C|Chrysalis}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* The randomization of {{BD|Confused}} or {{P|Snecko Oil}} will override the cost of the cards generated by this card.\n* Some {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat, or can only be obtained from another source.\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Alchemize}}\n* {{C|Wish}}\n* {{C|Bandage Up}}\n* {{C|Apparition}}\n* {{C|J.A.X.}}\n* {{C|Beta}}\n* {{C|Insight}}\n* {{C|Miracle}}\n* {{C|Safety}}\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like  Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Adding colorless card Chrysalis.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2063":{"pageid":2063,"ns":0,"title":"Cold Snap","revisions":[{"revid":56942,"parentid":55701,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Cold Snap\n|Image       = Blue-ColdSnap.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (6;9) damage. {{KW|Channel}} 1 {{KW|Frost}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Channel, Frost\n}}\n{{C|Cold Snap}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. <!---It deals 6 (9) damage, then {{KW|Channel|Channels}} 1 {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}}.--->\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n==== a) General Orb Synergies ====\n* Cold Snap works best with other Orb sources, such as {{C|Ball Lightning}} and {{C|Coolheaded}}, allowing Orbs to be {{KW|Evoke|Evoked}} more frequently. <!--- No idea what to include as prototypical orb gen cards, so just went with these two--->\n* {{C|Blizzard}} does more damage for each {{KW|Frost|Frost Orb}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} this combat.\n* Sources of {{BD|Focus}} will improve the effects of Orbs: {{C|Defragment}}, {{C|Consume}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, {{R|Data Disk}}\n* Sources of additional Orb Slots allow for having more [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]] in parallel: {{C|Capacitor}}, {{R|Runic Capacitor}}, {{R|Inserter}}, {{P|Potion of Capacity}}\n* {{C|Compile Driver}} draws a card for each unique type of Orb {{KW|Channel|Channeled}}.\n* {{C|Barrage}} deals damage for each {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} Orb, while {{C|Fission}} draws a card and adds 1 {{Icon|BE}} for each Channeled Orb.\n* {{C|Recursion}}, {{C|Dualcast}}, and {{C|Multi-Cast}} each can directly {{KW|Evoke}} your Orbs 1, 2, or X times respectively.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{C|Reprogram}} and {{C|Hyperbeam}} give negative {{BD|Focus}}, making Orbs generated by Cold Snap less effective.\n\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2266":{"pageid":2266,"ns":0,"title":"Creative AI","revisions":[{"revid":56950,"parentid":55711,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Creative AI\n|Image       = Blue-CreativeAI.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 3\n|CostPlus    = 2\n|Description = At the start of your turn, add a random Power card into your hand.\n|GivesToPlayer = Creative AI\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Creative AI\n|Image        = Icon CreativeAI.png\n|Description  = At the start of your turn, add X random {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} cards into your hand.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Intensity\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n}}\n{{C|Creative AI}} is a 3 (2 if upgraded) {{Icon|BE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives you one {{BD|Creative AI}}, which adds 1 {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card into your hand at the start of each turn. \n\n{{BD|Creative AI}} can only generate {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} cards you can find in card rewards through character choice or custom run modifiers, and is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Creative AI}} takes effect before your cards are drawn. This means that having a high amount of {{BD|Creative AI}} can cause you to draw less cards at the start of your turn due to the hand size limit.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with {{C|Storm}} and {{C|Heatsinks}} which get activated every time a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card is played. Both of these cards can also be generated by {{BD|Creative AI}}.\n* Synergizes with {{C|Force Field}}, as it ensures enough {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} will be available to eventually lower the cost of {{C|Force Field}} to 0, and already discounts it by 1 {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''' itself.\n* Synergizes extremely well with power-dependent relics, as {{R|Mummified Hand}} makes it easier to play all generated {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} cards, and {{R|Bird-Faced Urn}} allows you to heal to full HP if combat lasts long enough.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card generated by this card exceeds your hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n* Some {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} cards cannot be generated, as they have some permanent effect out of combat, or can only be obtained from another source.\n\n=== Excluded Cards ===\nAs with most random card generation effects, {{C|Creative AI}} cannot generate cards that are unobtainable from card rewards or cards that can heal the player. The following {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} will never be generated by {{C|Creative AI}}:\n* {{C|Self Repair}} (healing)\n* {{C|Omega}} (can only be generated during combat via {{C|Alpha}} and {{C|Beta}})\n* All {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless&type:Power|Colorless powers}} ({{C|Creative AI}} will only generate {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} of the player character's color and is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}})\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1943":{"pageid":1943,"ns":0,"title":"Dark Embrace","revisions":[{"revid":56768,"parentid":56767,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Dark Embrace\n| Image       = Red-DarkEmbrace.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 2\n| CostPlus    = 1\n| Description = Whenever a card is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}},<br>draw 1 card.\n| PowerGives = Draw, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Dark Embrace\n| Image        = Icon DarkEmbrace.png\n| Description  = Whenever a card is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}, draw X cards.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| InteractsWith = Exhaust\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}} \n{{C|Dark Embrace}} is a 2 (1 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 1 {{BD|Dark Embrace}}, which draws 1 card every time a card is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* When playing a card that {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} a card, {{BD|Dark Embrace}} draws ''after'' the played card is resolved. If the played card draws or adds cards to your hand, that will happen ''before'' {{BD|Dark Embrace}} is triggered. \n** For example, when bringing a card back with {{C|Exhume}}, it will place that card in your hand first, and only then draw cards through {{BD|Dark Embrace}}. This means that if your hand is full when playing that {{C|Exhume}}, it will still function as normal, and the draw of {{BD|Dark Embrace}} will be wasted.\n\n* {{KW|Ethereal}} cards {{KW|Exhaust}} at the end of your turn, but cards drawn through {{BD|Dark Embrace}} this way are not discarded, effectively giving you extra cards in hand next turn.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** (Undocumented) Rarity changed from Rare to Uncommon.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1939":{"pageid":1939,"ns":0,"title":"Dual Wield","revisions":[{"revid":56764,"parentid":50421,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Dual Wield\n|Image       = Red-DualWield.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Choose an Attack or Power card. Add (a copy;2 copies) of that card into your hand.\n}}\n\n{{C|Dual Wield}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It allows you to select one {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card in your hand, and add 1 copy (2 copies if upgraded) of that card into your hand.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Duplicating any card with \"Strike\" in its name using {{C|Dual Wield}} will increase the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}, as it counts all cards in your deck during combat, not your actual deck.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* When a card is copied, any changes to that card are also copied. The duration of these changes is initially the same for any copy as for the original. Once created, all copies behave fully independently.\n** A changed energy cost is copied, through something like {{R|Snecko Eye}}, {{C|Madness}} or {{P|Liquid Memories}}, or through the automatic energy change of cards like {{C|Blood for Blood}} and {{C|Masterful Stab}}.\n** Changes to the values of the card are copied, such as upgrades to {{C|Searing Blow}} or increased damage of {{C|Rampage}}.\n\n* If a copy created by {{C|Dual Wield}} exceeds the hand size limit, it gets added to the discard pile.\n\n== Bugs ==\n* While playing {{C|Dual Wield}} on {{C|Ritual Dagger}}, if the '''\"Choose a Card\"''' prompt opens, the original {{C|Ritual Dagger}} copy is lost, meaning any scaling it does within this combat will not be carried over outside of combat.\n** This can be prevented by making sure it is the only {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} or {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} card in hand, and therefore not opening the prompt. In this case, the leftmost {{C|Ritual Dagger}} is the original copy.\n\n* Under the effect of {{C|Master Reality}}, {{C|Dual Wield}} {{KW|Upgrade|Upgrades}} '''all''' cards, even the original card that was copied.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Update 40: Forethought'''\n** Card copy effects like Dual Wield should now also copy the \"free to play once\" effect from cards like Setup and Forethought.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 12: Lunar New Year'''\n** Copying cards from effects like Dual Wield now correctly displays cost as green if modified.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Dual Wield card is now Uncommon (was Common).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Dual Wield now properly works on ONLY Attacks and Powers as worded.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!'''\n** Dual Wield can no longer duplicate skills, stopping the easy infinites.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Dual Wield Card reworked and buffed.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1520":{"pageid":1520,"ns":0,"title":"Eviscerate","revisions":[{"revid":56347,"parentid":56346,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Eviscerate\n| Image       = Green-Eviscerate.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 3\n| Description = Costs 1 less {{Icon|GE}} for each card discarded this turn.<br>Deal (7;9) damage 3 times.\n| GivesToPlayer = Discard, Energy\n}}\n{{C|Eviscerate}} is a 3 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n{{TOC limit|3}}\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits 3 times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n\n* If {{C|Eviscerate}} costs 0 {{Icon|GE}} Energy, it will deal 3 times 4 extra damage from {{R|Wrist Blade}}. \n\n* If {{C|Eviscerate}} costs 2 or more {{Icon|GE}} Energy, it will be able to trigger {{R|Necronomicon}}.\n\n* Regardless of when it is drawn, {{C|Eviscerate}} will cost 1 less {{Icon|GE}} Energy per card that has previously been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]] in the same turn, in one of the following ways:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Survivor}}, {{C|Acrobatics}}, {{C|Dagger Throw}}, {{C|Prepared}}, {{C|Concentrate}}, {{C|Tools of the Trade}}, {{C|Unload}}.\n* {{C|All-Out Attack}}, although this risks discarding {{C|Eviscerate}}.\n* {{C|Calculated Gamble}}, if {{C|Eviscerate}} is drawn after playing it.\n* {{C|Storm of Steel}}, if {{C|Eviscerate}} is drawn after playing it, such as with {{R|Unceasing Top}} or {{C|Reflex}}.\n* {{C|Scrape}}.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Gambling Chip}}.\n* {{P|Gambler's Brew}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Cards moved to the discard pile through {{KW|Scry}} will not reduce the energy cost of {{C|Eviscerate}}.\n\n* {{C|Setup}}, {{C|Enlightenment}} and {{C|Forethought}} will reduce the cost to the specified number, after which the cost can possibly be further reduced by [[Keywords#Discard|discarding]] more cards. \n** These discounts apply regardless of whether {{C|Eviscerate}} is drawn or placed in hand through another card, unless this discount originated from an unupgraded version of {{C|Enlightenment}}.\n** If {{C|Eviscerate}} already costed 0, {{C|Enlightenment}} will not increase it to 1.\n\n* {{C|Eviscerate}} copied by {{C|Dual Wield}} will cost the same as the original, while the copies made by {{C|Nightmare}} the next turn will not include the discounted energy cost achieved by anything other than {{C|Setup}}, {{C|Forethought}} or upgraded {{C|Enlightenment}} in the current turn.\n\n* When drawn with {{R|Snecko Eye}} or {{P|Snecko Oil}} the cost will always be randomised regardless of how many cards have previously been [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]].\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* If '''Eviscerate''' is discounted through unupgraded {{C|Enlightenment}} or by [[Keywords#Discard|discarding]] cards, when it is fetched (example, with {{C|Secret Weapon}}), it will cost '''3'''.\n\n== Bugs ==\n\n=== Without Snecko Eye ===\n\n==== Infernal Blade ====\n* If {{C|Eviscerate}} is generated from {{C|Infernal Blade}}, its cost will be determined by the number of [[Keywords#Discard|Discards]] this turn. It will NOT be generated at 0 {{Icon|GE}} unless 3 cards are Discarded.\n\n* For example, if 2 cards are [[Keywords#Discard|Discarded]] before {{C|Infernal Blade}} is played, the cost of {{C|Eviscerate}} will be 1 {{Icon|GE}}.\n\n==== Fetched after Discard discount ====\n* When fetched by {{C|Secret Weapon}}, {{C|Violence}}, {{C|Seek}}, {{C|Hologram}}, Eviscerate will always cost 3 {{Icon|GE}}, even if it was discounted by Discards. \n\n* {{C|All for One}} will not pull the 0 {{Icon|GE}} costed (from 3 Discarded cards) Eviscerate.\n\n* Does not apply to discounted by {{C|Setup}}, {{C|Forethought}}, and upgraded {{C|Enlightenment}}, these work like normal.\n\n==== Soft discounts ====\n\nThese are discounts given by \n* {{C|Bullet Time}} \n* {{R|Mummified Hand}} \n* Unupgraded {{C|Enlightenment}} \n\nOr generated by \n* {{C|Foreign Influence}} \n* {{P|Attack Potion}}\n* {{C|Discovery}}\n\n===== a) Duplicating after soft discount =====\nIf a soft discounted Eviscerate is duplicated by {{C|Echo Form}}, {{P|Duplication Potion}} or {{C|Double Tap}}, it will cost 3 {{Icon|GE}} instead of 0 {{Icon|GE}} '''on the second play.'''\n\n===== b) Nightmare or Dual Wield after soft discount =====\nIf a soft discounted Eviscerate is played as a {{C|Nightmare}} target or {{C|Dual Wield}} target, it will return at 3 {{Icon|GE}} cost '''on the same turn'''.\n\n=== With Snecko Eye ===\n\n==== Calculated Gamble ====\n* Gambling into Eviscerate with Snecko Eye will make it cost 0 roughly 50%.\n\n* This is because the game has two types of cost: Permanent, and Temporary. When Eviscerate gets a discount through discards, the Temporary cost is changed. When Snecko Eye rolls for a cost and it matches the Permanent cost, it won't change Eviscerate's cost and Eviscerate will discount itself to 0 due to the Calculated Gamble.\n\n* Example: Eviscerate currently costs 3. When Calculated Gamble draws into it, it can cost 1 and 2 25% of the time. If the Snecko Eye cost rolls 3, it matches with Eviscerate's original cost and will discount itself to Calculated Gamble.\n\n===== a) Nightmare after Calculated Gamble =====\n* There is a chance that an Eviscerate that costs 0 after being Gambled into, when Nightmared, will not cost 0 next turn.\n* This is because Eviscerate will only retain the 0 cost if the cost was given by Snecko, and not if the cost was given by discards. There is no way to predict the cost of these copies.\n\n==== Nightmare or Dual Wield after soft discount ====\nIf Eviscerate discounted by {{C|Bullet Time}}, {{R|Mummified Hand}}, unupgraded {{C|Enlightenment}}, or generated by {{C|Foreign Influence}}, {{P|Attack Potion}}, {{C|Discovery}} is played as a {{C|Nightmare}} target or {{C|Dual Wield}} target, it will return at its original Snecko Eye {{Icon|GE}} cost '''on the same turn'''.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Eviscerate card buffed. Damage increased from 6 -> 7.\n** Eviscerate+ card buffed. Damage increased from 8 -> 9.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 45: Impatience'''\n** Fixes for how Eviscerate incorrectly worked with cost reduction effects like Enlightenment.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 25: Building Blocks'''\n** Eviscerate card now has correct cost when returned from Stasis power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** Eviscerate now correctly lowers cost by 1 per discard.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 9: Ascension'''\n** Fixed interaction of Enlightenment + Eviscerate + Discard.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!'''\n** Eviscerate's cost now correctly decreases when it is discarded.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!'''\n** Eviscerate now correctly works with the Confusion debuff.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1842":{"pageid":1842,"ns":0,"title":"Flying Knee","revisions":[{"revid":56392,"parentid":55787,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Flying Knee\n| Image       = Green-FlyingKnee.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal (8;11) damage.<br>Next turn, gain {{Icon|GE}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Energy\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Energized (Silent)}}\n{{C|Flying Knee}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 8 (11 if upgraded) damage and gives you 1 {{BD|Energized (Silent)}}, which gives you 1 extra {{Icon|GE}} '''Energy''' at the start of your next turn.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]] [[Category:ToUpdate]]"}}}]},"1931":{"pageid":1931,"ns":0,"title":"Pummel","revisions":[{"revid":56756,"parentid":55910,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Pummel\n| Image       = Red-Pummel.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal 2 damage (4;5) times.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Pummel}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 2 damage 4 (5 if upgraded) times. {{C|Pummel}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|The Boot}} increases the damage of each hit of this card to 5. \n* Benefits 4 (5 if upgraded) times from {{BD|Strength}} and {{BD|Vigor}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 31: Custom Mode'''\n** Optional UPGRADE_DESCRIPTION added for Pummel, Heavy Blade, Offering, and Reprogram\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1858":{"pageid":1858,"ns":0,"title":"Sentinel","revisions":[{"revid":56403,"parentid":55495,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Sentinel\n| Image       = Red-Sentinel.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Gain (5;8) {{KW|Block}}.<br>If this card is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}},<br>gain {{Icon|RE}}{{Icon|RE}}(;{{Icon|RE}}).\n| GivesToPlayer = Block, Energy\n| InteractsWith = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}} {{Keyword Infobox|Energy}}\n{{C|Sentinel}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 5 {{KW|Block}}. If {{C|Sentinel}} is {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}}, it will give 2 {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy''' instead.\n\n== Synergies ==\n=== Cards ===\n* Synergizes with any card that has a targeted {{KW|Exhaust}} or that {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} cards. Most notably, {{C|Corruption}} allows both effects of this card to be triggered.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2272":{"pageid":2272,"ns":0,"title":"Simmering Fury","revisions":[{"revid":55941,"parentid":50681,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Simmering Fury\n|Image       = Purple-SimmeringFury.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = At the start of your next turn, enter {{KW|Wrath}} and draw (2;3) cards.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Simmering Rage}}{{Power Infobox|Draw Card}}{{C|Simmering Fury}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives you one {{BD|Simmering Rage}}, which will make you enter the {{KW|Wrath}} {{KW|Stance}} at the start of your next turn. It also gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Draw Card}}, which will make you draw that amount of extra cards at the start of next turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Simmering Rage}} activates after {{BD|Mantra}} is given at the start of your turn. This means that if you get enough {{BD|Mantra}} to enter {{KW|Divinity}} through {{C|Devotion}} or {{R|Damaru}}, you will briefly enter {{KW|Divinity}} and then immediately enter {{KW|Wrath}}. This will give you the 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' benefit from entering {{KW|Divinity}}, and counts as two {{KW|Stance}} switches.\n\n* {{BD|Draw Card}} will activate after drawing cards regularly at the start of your turn, and after any possible {{BD|Rushdown}} draws cards as a result of having entered {{KW|Wrath}} through {{BD|Simmering Rage}}. This means that having excess {{BD|Draw Card}} will end up simply being wasted.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* When entering {{KW|Wrath}} if you are not in {{KW|Wrath}} yet:\n** If you have {{BD|Rushdown}} from {{C|Rushdown}}, you will draw that many cards.\n** You will switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n*** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n*** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n*** If you were in the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}} before, you will gain 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''', or 3 if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n* Being in {{KW|Wrath}} changes the effects of some cards:\n** {{C|Halt}} will give its additional {{KW|Block}}.\n** {{C|Indignation}} will apply {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* While in {{KW|Wrath}}, all {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} damage you deal is doubled, but you also take double damage from enemy attacks.{{KW|Wrath}} only doubles damage from {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, not from effects such as {{BD|Panache}} or {{BD|Thorns}}, or relics such as {{R|Mercury Hourglass}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{KW|Wrath}} is worse than the {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}} in every way except for the aformentioned ones, using {{C|Simmering Fury}} while in {{KW|Divinity}} is generally bad.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* In the game code, Simmering Fury is called Vengeance.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1815":{"pageid":1815,"ns":0,"title":"Tactician","revisions":[{"revid":56374,"parentid":55506,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Tactician\n| Image       = Green-Tactician.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = -2\n| Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>If this card is discarded from your hand, gain ({{Icon|GE}};{{Icon|GE}} {{Icon|GE}}).\n| GivesToPlayer = Discard, Energy, Unplayable\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Unplayable}}\n{{C|Tactician}} is an unplayable {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n'''Tactician''' does nothing unless [[Keywords#Discard|discarded]], in one of the following ways:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Survivor}}, {{C|Acrobatics}}, {{C|Dagger Throw}}, {{C|Prepared}}, {{C|Calculated Gamble}}, {{C|Concentrate}}, {{C|Tools of the Trade}},{{C|Storm of Steel}}, {{C|Unload}}.\n* {{C|All-Out Attack}}, although this cannot reliably target {{C|Tactician}}.\n* {{C|Scrape}}.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Gambling Chip}}.\n* {{P|Gambler's Brew}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Tactician card is now Uncommon.\n** Improved formatting for Tactician and Ritual Dagger cards.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** We removed one level of unlocks! Three additional cards are now available by default in the card pool for both The Silent and Ironclad. The following cards are now added to the card pool by default: Underhanded Strike, Reflex, Tactician\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Tactician card buff.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1894":{"pageid":1894,"ns":0,"title":"Uppercut","revisions":[{"revid":56428,"parentid":55991,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Uppercut\n| Image       = Red-Uppercut.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Deal 13 damage.<br>Apply (1;2) {{BD|Weak}}.<br>Apply (1;2) {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n| GivesToEnemy = Weak, Vulnerable\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Weak}}{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}}{{C|Uppercut}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 13 damage and applies 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Weak}} and 1 (2 if upgraded) {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* The {{BD|Weak}} applies first and the {{BD|Vulnerable}} applies afterwards, meaning enemies with one {{BD|Artifact}} will only receive the {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Paper Phrog}} increases the effectiveness of {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2478":{"pageid":2478,"ns":0,"title":"Violence","revisions":[{"revid":50753,"parentid":36953,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Violence\n|Image       = Colorless-Violence.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Put (3;4) random Attacks from your draw pile into your hand.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Violence}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It puts 3 (4 if upgraded) {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards, randomly chosen from your draw pile, into your hand for as long as there is still space in hand. It then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} itself.\n\n== Obtaining Violence ==\n{{C|Violence}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 38: Bane'''\n** Adding colorless card Violence.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2375":{"pageid":2375,"ns":0,"title":"Wish","revisions":[{"revid":55644,"parentid":55189,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Wish\n|Image       = Purple-Wish.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 3\n|Description = Choose one:<br>Gain (6;8) {{BD|Plated Armor}}, (3;4) {{BD|Strength}}, or (25;30) Gold. {{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{C|Wish}} is a 3 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives the choice between 3 cards, of which the chosen one gets played immediately:\n* {{C|Live Forever}}, which gives 6 (8 if {{C|Wish}} was upgraded) {{BD|Plated Armor}}\n* {{C|Become Almighty}}, which gives 3 (4 if {{C|Wish}} was upgraded) {{BD|Strength}}\n* {{C|Fame and Fortune}}, which gives 25 (30 if {{C|Wish}} was upgraded) [[Gold]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Despite the fact that {{C|Wish}} technically creates a card, {{C|Master Reality}} does NOT upgrade that card. Upgrading {{C|Wish}} itself is the only way to upgrade the cards that it creates.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{C|Wish}} is the only card in the game that creates, then immediately plays a card. The three cards that {{C|Wish}} creates never enter your hand and cannot be added to the deck.\n* The beta design of '''Become Almighty''' is a reference to All Might, a character from My Hero Academia.\n\n{{Clear}}\n== Options ==\n<tabber>\n|-| Live Forever =\n<span id=\"Live Forever\"></span>\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Live Forever\n|Image       = Colorless-LiveForever.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = -2\n|Description = Gain (6;8) {{BD|Plated Armor}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Plated Armor}}\n{{C|Live Forever}} is an unplayable {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It can only be obtained and played through {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher's}} {{C|Wish}}. It gives 6 (8 if upgraded through playing an upgraded {{C|Wish}}) {{BD|Plated Armor}}. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Plated Armor}} gives {{KW|Block}} after {{R|Orichalcum}} checks if you have block.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} gained by {{BD|Plated Armor}} is unaffected by {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|No Block}} from a previously played {{C|Panic Button}}.\n\n|-| Become Almighty =\n<span id=\"Become Almighty\"></span>\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Become Almighty\n|Image       = Colorless-BecomeAlmighty.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = -2\n|Description = Gain (3;4) {{BD|Strength}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Strength}}\n{{C|Become Almighty}} is an unplayable {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It can only be obtained and played through {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher's}} {{C|Wish}}. It gives 3 (4 if upgraded through playing an upgraded {{C|Wish}}) {{BD|Strength}}. \n\n|-| Fame and Fortune =\n<span id=\"Fame and Fortune\"></span>\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Fame and Fortune\n|Image       = Colorless-FameandFortune.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Special\n|Cost        = -2\n|Description = Gain (25;30) Gold\n}}\n{{C|Fame and Fortune}} is an unplayable {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It can only be obtained and played through {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher's}} {{C|Wish}}. It gives 25 (30 if upgraded through playing an upgraded {{C|Wish}}) gold. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Positive ===\n* {{R|Bloody Idol}} heals for 5 HP when [[Gold]] is collected.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{R|Ectoplasm}} will fully negate the effect of this card.\n\n</tabber>\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1824":{"pageid":1824,"ns":0,"title":"Wraith Form","revisions":[{"revid":56613,"parentid":56381,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Wraith Form\n| Image       = Green-WraithForm.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 3\n| Description = Gain (2;3) {{BD|Intangible}}.<br>At the end of your turn, lose 1 {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Intangible, Wraith Form\n| PowerGives = Dexterity (Negative)\n}} \n{{Power Infobox|Intangible}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Wraith Form\n| Image        = Icon WraithForm.png\n| Description  = At the start of your turn, lose X {{BD|Dexterity}}.\n| Type         = Debuff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToPlayer = Dexterity (Negative)\n}}\n{{C|Wraith Form}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It costs 3 {{Icon|GE}} Energy to play and provides the player with 2 (3) stacks of {{BD|Intangible}}. While the player has {{BD|Intangible}}, every instance of damage taken is reduced to 1.\n\nHowever, {{C|Wraith Form}} also afflicts the player with the {{BD|Wraith Form}} debuff, which reduces the player's {{BD|Dexterity}} by 1 each turn for the remainder of combat or until the debuff is removed.\n\n== Synergies ==\n\n=== Cards ===\n\n* The {{BD|Wraith Form}} debuff can be prevented by gaining {{BD|Artifact}} through {{C|Core Surge}} or {{C|Panacea}}. See [[#Interactions|Interactions]] below. \n* {{BD|Dexterity}} sources such as {{C|Footwork}} and potentially {{C|Reprogram}} or {{C|Fasting}} can be used to temporarily counteract ongoing {{BD|Dexterity}} reduction from {{BD|Wraith Form}}. \n* {{BD|Intangible}} provided from {{C|Apparition}} will stack on top of any {{BD|Intangible}} gained through {{C|Wraith Form}}. \n* {{C|Wraith Form}} is a strong {{C|Nightmare}} target, giving the player access to substantially more stacks of {{BD|Intangible}}. However, playing '''X''' {{C|Wraith Form|Wraith Forms}} causes the {{BD|Wraith Form}} debuff to stack, reducing '''X''' {{BD|Dexterity}} each turn.\n* {{C|Well-Laid Plans}} can be used to {{KW|Retain}} {{C|Wraith Form}} until an optimal turn, such as an especially high-damage enemy attack, to maximise damage reduction.\n* Self-damage cards such as {{C|Offering}} and {{C|Hemokinesis}} will only reduce the player's HP by 1 while {{BD|Intangible}} is active. \n\n=== Relics === \n\n* {{R|Tungsten Rod}} reduces all HP loss to 0 while the player has {{BD|Intangible}}. \n* Sources of {{BD|Dexterity}} such as {{R|Kunai}} and to a lesser extent {{R|Oddly Smooth Stone}} can also counteract the {{BD|Dexterity}} loss induced by {{BD|Wraith Form}}.\n* The {{BD|Wraith Form}} debuff can be '''entirely cleansed''' using {{R|Orange Pellets}}. Since {{C|Wraith Form}} is itself a Power, playing an Attack and a Skill the same turn as it will activate {{R|Orange Pellets}} and clear all debuffs, including {{BD|Wraith Form}}. \n* The {{BD|Artifact}} provided by {{R|Clockwork Souvenir}} at the start of combat can be used to nullify the {{BD|Wraith Form}} debuff. Since the relic always activates at the very start of combat, its {{BD|Artifact}} will always nullify {{BD|Wraith Form}} entirely when {{C|Wraith Form}} is played instead of doing so for just one turn (see [[#Interactions|Interactions]]).\n\n=== Potions ===\n\n* {{P|Ancient Potion}} can provide {{BD|Artifact}}, which will nullify the {{BD|Wraith Form}} debuff if used ''before'' {{C|Wraith Form}} is played (see [[#Interactions|Interactions]] below). \n* {{P|Dexterity Potion}} can temporarily counteract the {{BD|Dexterity}} loss induced by {{BD|Wraith Form}}. \n* {{P|Ghost in a Jar}} can also provide 1 stack of {{BD|Intangible}} (2 with {{R|Sacred Bark}}) which is additive with {{BD|Intangible}} gained from {{C|Wraith Form}}. \n\n=== Power-based ===\nBeing a Power, it will:\n\n* '''Heal''' for '''2''' with {{R|Bird-Faced Urn}}.\n* Make a random card cost 0 temporarily with {{R|Mummified Hand}}.\n* Draw '''X''' cards with '''X''' stacks of {{C|Heatsinks}}.\n* Generate '''X''' {{Icon|LO}} '''Lightning Orbs''' with '''X''' stacks of {{C|Storm}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Artifacts === \n\n{{BD|Artifact}} can be used to prevent the {{BD|Wraith Form}} debuff, but will only cleanse the debuff in full if acquired ''before'' {{C|Wraith Form}} is played.\n\nIf '''X''' {{BD|Artifact}} is acquired ''after'' the player already has the {{BD|Wraith Form}} debuff, the next '''X''' instances of {{BD|Dexterity}} loss will be prevented, but the debuff itself will not be cleansed.\n\nThis interaction applies regardless of how {{BD|Artifact}} is gained, whether through cards, relics, or potions. \n\n=== Thorns and Beat of Death ===\n\n* While {{BD|Intangible}}, [[Corrupt Heart]]'s {{BD|Beat of Death}} deals only 1 damage each time a card is played.\n* [[Guardian]]'s {{BD|Sharp Hide}} and [[Shapes#Spiker|Spikers]]' {{BD|Thorns}} will only deal 1 damage while {{BD|Intangible}} is active.\n\n=== Other sources of Intangible ===\n\nAcquiring {{BD|Intangible}} through other means, such as {{C|Apparition}} or {{P|Ghost in a Jar}}, will increment {{BD|Intangible}} stacks provided by {{C|Wraith Form}} and vice versa.\n\n=== Enemy intents ===\n\nIf an enemy is attacking while the player has {{BD|Intangible}}, their intent will be updated to show 1 damage per hit. Multi-hits will be converted to 1 times X damage, where X is the number of hits the enemy intends to inflict. \n\n=== Sources of Block unaffected by Dexterity === \n\nThe {{BD|Wraith Form}} debuff has no effect on sources of {{KW|Block}} that do not scale with {{BD|Dexterity}}. These include:\n\n* {{P|Block Potion}}\n* {{C|After Image}}\n* {{C|Feel No Pain}}\n* {{C|Mental Fortress}}\n* {{C|Nirvana}}\n* {{C|Like Water}}\n* {{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}}\n* {{R|Ornamental Fan}}\n* {{R|Orichalcum}} \n* {{R|Anchor}}, {{R|Horn Cleat}}, and {{R|Captain's Wheel}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n\n* {{C|Wraith Form}}, {{C|Biased Cognition}}, and {{C|Fasting}} are the only Power cards in the game that afflict the player with a '''persistent''' debuff. {{C|Berserk|Berserk's}} {{BD|Vulnerable}} debuff is capped at 2 turns (1 if upgraded). \n* {{C|Wraith Form|Wraith Form's}} Beta Art was prominently featured on the [https://contentiongames.myshopify.com/products/slay-the-spire-beta-art-cards Beta Art expansion box] of [https://contentiongames.com/games/slay/ Slay the Spire: The Board Game].\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}